```
Wait the last cap: from (-straight, -halfDepth) around the left end to (-straight, +halfDepth): angles from -π/2 to -3π/2 (i.e., decreasing) → a = -π/2 - π*i/12; at i=12 → -3π/2 → (x=-straight + 0, z = +halfDepth) ✓ which closes to the first point. So loop i=1..11 to avoid duplicating the first point.

Check the side(-1) loop: at i=1, t=1-1/12 → x = straight - 2*straight/12..., starts near (straight, -halfDepth) — but the right cap already ended at (straight,-halfDepth) ✓ so push dedupes the first.

Order/winding: fine.

